  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Consider, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>PF</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>BrF</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>PCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>SF</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msub><mi>ICl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ClF</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>IF</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math></p><p>Amongst the above molecule(s) ion(s), the number of molecule(s)/ion(s) having <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> hybridisation is</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Number of hybrid orbitals = Number of bond pair + number of lone pair on central atom.</p><p>To have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;hybridisation there should be total of 6 (bond pairs + lone pairs). The structure in such case will be octahedral or its derivative structures.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/fdb78405-51a3-4feb-9954-0f62ed23d690-993f7d80-abbd-4917-8eae-e4bac022163f-image.png\" style=\"width: 324px; height: 458px;\" /></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/7b2bff78-da63-4143-99b3-e0bcbb66ef66-9e3bfbe6-4f29-4113-adf7-b70e242753b6-image.png\" style=\"width: 296px; height: 394px;\" /></p></blockquote>",
